#N canvas 0 0 760 860 10;
#X text 12 8 sid-player - a PSID file through one sid~ + one sid6581~ (each voice scoped);
#X text 12 28 sid~ runs the tune's own 6502 player code: outlet 0 emits `reg <a> <d>` for every $D400-$D418 write \, plus `clock <Hz>` and `model <6581|8580>` on load (the chip configures itself from the file header when the file carries one). VBI tunes play at the video frame rate \, CIA tunes at the timer rate their own code programs - demo.sid is a CIA tune (50.12 Hz).;
#X text 12 60 sid6581~ is the whole chip (reSID engine): outlet 0 = the chip's AUDIO OUT (filter + output stage) \, outlets 1-3 = voices 1-3 alone. The mix is NOT clipped internally - the sum can reach ~3 - so the final gain owns the headroom (this patch: 0.3).;
#X text 12 92 Seekrank_und_Skorbut.sid and ZeckenSID.sid ship with the examples: two full three-voice SID tunes by Jan Wassermann aka Spider Jerusalem of Mayday \, from the CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 collection A Lazy Year for the 8580 chip \, csdb.dk release 160991. These v1 files carry no model field - press model 8580 after loading them. demo.sid is also bundled - a hand-assembled A-minor loop with pulse lead \, saw bass and noise drums (6581). Put your own .sid next to a patch or anywhere on the pd search path. RSID files are rejected - they need real interrupt handlers.;
#X msg 40 140 load Seekrank_und_Skorbut.sid;
#X msg 280 140 load ZeckenSID.sid;
#X msg 470 140 load demo.sid;
#X msg 40 168 model 8580;
#X msg 140 168 model 6581;
#X msg 240 168 play;
#X msg 300 168 pause;
#X msg 360 168 stop;
#X msg 420 168 info;
#X text 40 200 one chip \, three voices - the scopes show what each part of the tune contributes;
#X obj 40 260 sid~;
#X obj 40 310 sid6581~;
#X obj 40 360 *~ 0.3;
#X text 110 360 gain fits the three-voice sum (~1.0 on the demo) - lower it further if dac~ still clips;
#X obj 40 410 dac~;
#X obj 40 470 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 470 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 480 470 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 40 580 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 260 590 scopes: chip mix (top left) and voices 1-3;
#X text 12 660 the tune loops forever (SID format has no end marker) - press stop to silence it. subtune <n> switches tunes on multi-tune files.;
#X connect 4 0 14 0;
#X connect 5 0 14 0;
#X connect 6 0 14 0;
#X connect 7 0 15 0;
#X connect 8 0 15 0;
#X connect 9 0 14 0;
#X connect 10 0 14 0;
#X connect 11 0 14 0;
#X connect 12 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 15 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 1;
#X connect 16 0 18 0;
#X connect 16 0 18 1;
#X connect 15 0 19 0;
#X connect 15 1 20 0;
#X connect 15 2 21 0;
#X connect 15 3 22 0;
